WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.734
-Bashir, Diallo!
-What's up?

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.234
-It is always great
to see you guys.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.434
Congratulations, by the way.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:06.934
I want to talk about
"Sherman's Showcase."

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:09.434
It is so funny and so awesome.

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:11.901
We talked about this when you
were on the show once before.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:14.767
You guys were once writers
for our show,

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.400
for me at "Late Night."
-Yeah.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.000
-And you wrote
some of the best bits

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.734
that we've ever done
on our show.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:20.901
So thank you for those bits.

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:22.434
And I mean,
"History of Hip-Hop."

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:23.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.367
Endless.
-Yeah.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.601
-And it's cool to see --
it's cool to see you guys

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:31.400
get your own show and crush it,
by the way.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.267
100% fresh on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.901
Not too shabby, bud.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.901
The reviews for season two --

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.067
let me just read a couple
of these, and, oh, yeah, yeah.

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:42.901
"Daily Beast" says
"TV's coolest variety show

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:44.834
makes its triumphant return."

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
"Sherman's Showcase."

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:50.267
New York Times says,
"This musical comedy tribute

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:53.701
to Black culture has returned
as joyfully absurd as ever."

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:57.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Ooh!

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.634
That's got to feel --
that's got to feel good.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.100
I mean, you put
so much work into it.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.100
But, Bashir, you were telling me
backstage that it came from

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.701
a sketch
that we did on our show?

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.467
-You know, Jimmy, it's important
always to give you credit.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.667
-No, no, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:10.901
-It's a condition of appearing
on this show.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.100
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.667
I make everyone give me credit
for their career.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.100
-No, but seriously, man.
I mean, you let us have

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.434
so much fun
when we worked with you.

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:18.234
You let us do our thing.
And one of the sketches we did,

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:19.767
'cause you know we love music,

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:22.501
was Jackie Neptune
and The Planetariums,

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:23.667
which is a --
-Oh, I remember that.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.167
-That's right.
It was a solar body-obsessed

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:26.834
R&amp;B group that sang soul.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.501
And at the end of every song,
they'd be like...

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.000
♪ Planetariums ♪

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.501
-Yes, yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:33.467
Jackie Neptune.
-But the science checked out.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:36.000
Like, we always made sure
that all the science involved

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.200
in the --
-Oh, you did your research.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.467
-Oh, yeah, absolutely.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.934
I mean, as much research
as you can get off of Wikipedia.

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:40.934
-Yeah.
-Sure.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.200
-But it was --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.434
-In a hurried afternoon
before the sketch airs.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:45.801
-I have a photo of, actually...
-Let's go.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:46.834
-...you guys performing
Jackie --

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:47.901
-There's a photo?
-Yeah.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.534
Jackie Neptune
and The Planetariums.

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.300
Here.
-Oh, man.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.868
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:54.968
Look at that.

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.701
-I remember
I wanted my guy to have --

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:58.334
I wanted him to be a redhead.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.667
I wanted him to be, like,
a Black guy with red hair.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:01.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:02.934
-I think Kirk
is over there on the --

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.000
-There's Kirk.
-Kirk, yeah.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.667
-Tariq's hair is the best.
-Tariq.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.167
-Right in the middle.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.601
-That's nice, right there.
-So smooth.

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.234
-So, you finished that.
And after this sketch,

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.534
you said to Diallo, you're like,
"Hey" --

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.300
-Yeah, we were talking
literally right in this hallway,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.801
and then -- yeah, we were
just talking about how --

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.400
-I mean, like, we were sitting
out in the hallway, I was like,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.033
"Bashir, honestly, like,
we have to find out --

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:23.067
we have to find our way to do a
show where it's just this."

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.534
-Yeah.
-"Where it's just us in wigs,

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.300
and we write original songs."
-Yep.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.767
-"And just have so much fun."

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:29.767
And, honestly, me and him,
we've known each other forever,

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:32.200
so there were some song ideas
that we had that were

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.367
not quite appropriate for NBC.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:35.601
A little dark.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:36.968
-We didn't want to put you
in that position.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.400
-Yeah.
-I appreciate that.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.100
Thank you
for looking out for me.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.934
But how did you pitch it to IFC?
-Oh, it was --

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:45.100
Man, honestly, it was the
easiest pitch we've ever had,

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.501
I think, ever.
We went into the place

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:48.901
where we ended up
making the show.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:52.734
And we told them, you know,
what "30 Rock" is to "SNL,"

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.901
this show is gonna be
to "Soul Train."

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:56.067
-That's right.
-And they were like --

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:57.534
We got, like, 30 seconds in,
they're like,

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.667
"We're making the show."
-Wow.

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.567
-"Now tell us how to" --
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:03.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
That doesn't happen every time.

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.601
-And the premise --

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:10.167
The premise is Sherman
has his own variety show.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:11.868
-That's right.
Saturday mornings.

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:14.434
-Saturday mornings.
-Right after "Jabberjaw."

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:15.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:17.234
It's "Jabberjaw,"
and then "Sherman."

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:19.767
But why the '70s?
And why --

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.767
-Well, you know,
we like the variety format.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.701
You know, they don't happen
as much nowadays,

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:27.400
but there was a time in the '70s
when everybody had a vari--

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.667
Rerun from "What's Happening!!"

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.133
They were like,
"Hey, you want a variety show?"

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:33.334
He was like, "Yes."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.234
-Very -- yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Thank you.

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:37.100
[ Laughter ]
-Everyone had one.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.701
-Dance of the '70s, thank you.
-Yeah.

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:40.300
-Paramore fans are like,
"What is he doing?"

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.234
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.868
-It's a long story.
But, no, everybody had a show,

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.734
and it was a chance
to do music and comedy.

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.400
And for us, it was like,
"Well, let's use that

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.901
as the baseline for the show

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:52.234
because then we can do sketches
about anything in the world,"

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:53.901
and any music that we do can
happen on that stage,

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:55.234
and we can just
have a lot of fun.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.200
-And then you made Sherman --
you said he's kind of

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.934
a little bit based on, like,
Krusty the Clown?

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.234
-Yeah, he's based
on Krusty the Clown.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:01.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:04.400
You know, I love Krusty.
He's the ultimate showman.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.634
Like Krusty,
Sherman has no allegiances.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.701
He literally will stab
anybody in the back

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:12.200
if it helps him for one second.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.267
-He stabbed my character
in the back.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:14.634
-Many times.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.434
He literally was like,
"You got to go," yeah.

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.167
-Yeah, he actually has.

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:19.968
But you got John Legend
to produce.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.801
-Yeah, yeah.
I mean, yeah.

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:23.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
He's a great guy now.

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:25.100
-He's a good --
-Did you hear that, John?

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.400
You finally got some applause.
-Finally.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.267
Finally, somebody says something
about John Legend.

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:30.834
-Finally.
-Finally.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:32.534
Said his name on TV.
-Wow, he's a big --

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:35.200
A big shot now.
-You know what's funny?

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.501
John and I had a mutual friend,

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:40.734
and my wife was having
our second child's baby shower.

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:42.067
-Yeah.
-And John and Chrissy came,

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.968
and then Chrissy and Brittany --
my wife, Brittany --

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.601
they hit it off,
and they were friends.

00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:47.667
So John and I were
at parties together and, like --

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.701
we were always like,
"Hey, we want to work together."

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:52.167
And then, eventually, you know,
came this show

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.434
that married music with comedy,

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:56.434
and we knew that John
dabbled in music.

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:57.501
-Sure.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.501 --> 00:05:00.734
-Sort of a side hustle of his.
And --

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.200
And it was just
a really cool thing.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.000
But, you know, what's
interesting about that is that,

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.033
like, in some ways,
for that reason, like,

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:08.767
the show would not exist
without my wife,

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.200
who's also the choreographer
on the show --

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.701
-That's right.
-I think it's --

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:12.834
-Shout-out, Brittany Riddle.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:14.934
-Brittany.

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:16.701
-Brittany wrote all those dances
you see on the show.

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:17.834
Those are her work.

00:05:17.834 --> 00:05:20.434
It's very much a family affair.
-It is.

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.434
-But my nephew
does the animation.

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:23.934
His sister
is one of the writers.

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:25.501
She actually wrote --
She brought us the idea.

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:27.400
She's like, "I've got this idea
for 'Drop It Low for Jesus.'"

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.501
-That's right.
-And we were like --

00:05:29.501 --> 00:05:31.033
-And America's
never been the same.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:34.667
-And Amer-- I hired extra --
-"Drop It Low for Jesus."

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.033
-"Drop It Low --"
"Drop It Low for Jesus."

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:37.267
-Of course.
I understood.

00:05:37.267 --> 00:05:39.000
-I heard this thing --
Diallo, is this true?

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.767
I heard that you
just sometimes cast people,

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:42.667
like, on the street.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.367
-Yes, he does.
-Yes, I do.

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:45.501
-Who?
-Okay.

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:47.501
So, on our show,
we have a security guard.

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:48.834
His name is Reynard.

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:51.133
And there's just one day
that I was in Vegas,

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:53.801
and it's this typical --
You know, it's a Sunday morning,

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:56.601
and, you know,
might be a little hungover.

00:05:56.601 --> 00:05:57.567
Kids, turn this off.

00:05:57.567 --> 00:05:58.701
-Maybe had one or two cocktails.

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:00.200
-Yeah, one or two.
-Maybe, maybe.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.100
-It's Las Vegas.
I needed fried food.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.000
So, I went to --
So, I went to --

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.601
This shows you
the condition I was in.

00:06:06.601 --> 00:06:09.000
I went to the Walmart stooper --
superstore.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.167
-Yeah.
-By the way, I probably

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.868
called it the "stooper store"
at the time.

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:13.400
I went to the Walmart
superstore.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.734
You got to go -- have to go off
The Strip to find this Walmart.

00:06:15.734 --> 00:06:17.267
And the guy --
-In Vegas?

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:18.567
-In Vegas!
-You went to a Walmart?

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.734
I just -- Look, they have
a particular type of chicken

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.868
that's fantastic.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:24.133
-I've never heard this!

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:25.968
-Why does it always have
to be about the chicken for you?

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:27.534
-I don't know.
-I --

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:29.033
[ Laughter ]
-I have a problem.

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.501
-Not okay.
-But I walked up to the counter

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:34.300
where you order the food,
and this -- this old Black guy

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.400
came up there,
and he had me cracking up.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.033
Like, you know how, like,
sometimes, like,

00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:39.868
you're struggling,
but then somebody

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:41.868
just comes along and they're
just cracking you up?

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.067
-Yeah.
-And I was standing there,

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:44.734
and all I wanted was chicken,
but I was crying.

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:47.501
I was -- I was crying.
I was dead, I was dying.

00:06:47.501 --> 00:06:49.667
And I was like,
"My man, what's your name?"

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:50.801
And he was like, "Reynard."

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:52.167
And I was like,
"You are so funny.

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:54.167
One of these days, if I can ever
find a part for you --"

00:06:54.167 --> 00:06:56.067
I was like, "Do you act?"
And he was like, "Not really."

00:06:56.067 --> 00:06:57.501
I was like, "Doesn't matter."

00:06:57.501 --> 00:06:59.100
I was like,
"You're a funny person."

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.467
We do this on "South Side," too.
-Yeah.

00:07:00.467 --> 00:07:02.234
-If we find somebody
who's just funny, we're just,

00:07:02.234 --> 00:07:03.734
like, we'll put them
on the show.

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:07.267
And so, now, two seasons later,
Reynard the security guard...

00:07:07.267 --> 00:07:08.968
-Yeah.
-...is Sherman's security guard.

00:07:08.968 --> 00:07:10.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:12.634
It is so funny.

00:07:12.634 --> 00:07:14.934
Don't stop crushing.
Keep crushing.

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:16.167
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:16.167 --> 00:07:18.300
Here are Bashir Salahuddin
and Diallo Riddle

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.133
in the new season of
"Sherman's Showcase."

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:21.567
Take a look at this.

00:07:21.567 --> 00:07:25.267
-Attention passengers -- we have
taken control of the ship.

00:07:28.501 --> 00:07:31.968
Hand over Sherman McDaniels
and no one has to die --

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:33.501
violently, that is.
[ Crowd gasps ]

00:07:33.501 --> 00:07:36.100
Also, this is Ngasi speaking.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.834
I know what you are thinking.

00:07:37.834 --> 00:07:40.667
I died in the
Black History Month Special,

00:07:40.667 --> 00:07:43.434
but I survived, and I'm back.

00:07:43.434 --> 00:07:46.033
-Well, folks, if Reynard is not
successful with his crowbar,

00:07:46.033 --> 00:07:47.334
it looks like
we're all going to die.

00:07:47.334 --> 00:07:48.634
[ Crowd gasps ]
So, for those of you

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.167
who have something to live for,
I apologize.

00:07:50.167 --> 00:07:51.234
For the rest,
I'll see you in hell.

00:07:51.234 --> 00:07:53.267
Dutch?

00:07:53.267 --> 00:07:54.734
-Let me go negotiate with him.

00:07:54.734 --> 00:07:56.667
You stay here
and keep the show going.

00:07:56.667 --> 00:07:59.667
-Dutch, no.
It could be dangerous.

00:07:59.667 --> 00:08:01.267
-Sherman, I didn't know you --
-You're wasting time, brother.

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:02.300
You're wasting time.
I'll do it.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:04.400
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:07.567
-Bashir Salahuddin,
Diallo Riddle, everybody!

00:08:07.567 --> 00:08:09.767
Season two
of "Sherman's Showcase"

00:08:09.767 --> 00:08:13.667
airs Wednesdays at 10:30 p.m.
on IFC.

